    directly related to their business where it is not of a professional character for them.
  </p>
  <ol class={OL}>
    <li>
      <strong>Right of withdrawal.</strong> A Consumer may withdraw from a distance contract
      within 14 days of the day it was concluded, without giving any reason, subject to
      paragraph 4.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How to withdraw.</strong> To withdraw, it is enough to send the Provider an
      unequivocal statement before the period expires, for example by email to
      <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. The
      <a href="#withdrawal-form">model withdrawal form</a> at the end of these terms may be used,
      but it is not obligatory.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Effects of withdrawal.</strong> If the Consumer validly withdraws, the Provider
      reimburses all payments received from the Consumer without undue delay and no later than
      14 days from the day the statement was received. The refund is made using the same means
      of payment the Consumer used, unless the Consumer expressly agrees otherwise; the Consumer
      bears no costs of the refund.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Early expiry of the right of withdrawal.</strong> The Book is digital content not
      supplied on a tangible medium, produced to the Consumer's own specification, and
      Generation starts immediately after payment. Before paying, the Consumer, by ticking the
      corresponding box, expressly requests that performance begin before the withdrawal period
      ends and acknowledges that <strong>they lose the right of withdrawal once Generation of
      the Book begins</strong> (Article 16(m) of Directive 2011/83/EU; in Poland Article
      38(1)(13) of the Act of 30 May 2014 on consumer rights; in Germany § 356(5) of the German
      Civil Code, BGB). Payment is not possible without ticking that box.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Confirmation.</strong> The Consumer receives confirmation of the contract,
      including the wording of the statement referred to in paragraph 4 and the time it was
      made, on a durable medium — in the order confirmation email. This information is also
      printed on the payment receipt.
    </li>
    <li>
      Because Generation starts straight after payment, in practice the contract can no longer
      be withdrawn from once the payment has been made. This is why the title, the table of
      contents and the chapter sample (§3(2)) are provided free of charge before purchase, so
      that the Book can be assessed before paying.
    </li>
    <li>
      Losing the right of withdrawal does not limit the Consumer's rights where the digital
      content does not conform with the contract, the right to complain (§11), or the right to
      a refund in the case described in §7(3).
    </li>
  </ol>

